Appendix E — Architecture Specifications

E.1 Layer interfaces

L0 (Embodiment abstraction). Input: URDF/SDF, actuator datasheets, sensor specifications, compute constraints. Output: UBI record \mathcal D_i=(\sigma_i,\hat{\mathbf c}_i,\Sigma_i,\Gamma_i,h_i,\kappa_i,J\text{-cert}_i). The J-certificate is the empirical estimate of J(\hat P_{ik}) that certifies A4.

L1 (Runtime assurance). Input: x,u_{\mathrm{nom}},f_i,g_i,\delta_i,h_i. Output: u_{\mathrm{safe}} or a feasibility-violation event. The layer has no access to the learner’s internal state.

L2 (Adaptation). Input: source policy \pi_i, target body B_j, adaptation data \mathcal D_n. Output: adapted policy \pi_j^{(n)}. The learner is a Strategy object; swapping RL for VLA does not change L3.

L3 (Prediction). Input: UBI records for B_i,B_j, learner identifier \mathcal L, task \tau. Output: \widehat{\log N^\star} with a censoring-adjusted conformal interval and a discordant-cell support flag.

L4 (Pre-registration). Immutable Specification objects for thresholds (m_1,m_2,\varrho_{\max},\eta,R_{\min},\rho_{\min}); any deviation is logged.

E.2 Algorithm 4 (verification-cost decomposition)

```
Input: target body B_j, barrier h_j
Output: V_model, V_margin, V_calibration

1. V_model ← cost to identify (f_j, g_j, δ_j) until ||δ_j|| ≤ δ_max
2. V_margin ← cost to reach μ_j > 0 given the identified model
3. V_calibration ← cost to calibrate the filter on the target
4. if μ_j ≤ 0 after V_model:
       return (V_model, ∞, ∞)   // qualitative transfer-cost event
5. return (V_model, V_margin, V_calibration)
```

The separation of the three components is not cosmetic: a filter that is feasible only after extensive model identification is a different engineering object from one that is feasible out of the box, and the difference is exactly what a transfer-cost framework should capture. The Observer pattern on L1 emits a qualitative event when \mu_j\le0, so that the vacuous guarantee is recorded as data rather than silently degrading.

E.3 The J-certificate

For each scalar marginal \hat P_{ik}^\tau, the certificate is

\hat J_{ik}=\int_0^1\sqrt{\hat F_{ik}^{-1}(q)\big(1-\hat F_{ik}^{-1}(q)\big)}\,dq,

computed on the empirical quantile function. The certificate fails A4 if \hat J_{ik} is infinite or exceeds a pre-registered J_{\max}. Without the certificate, Lemma 1 and Corollary 5 do not apply, and the probe is not admissible as an input to L3.

